---
intent: >
  Strip every brain-writing surface out of the cold-start CLI. After this
  plan, `runInit` ships only the methodology layer — methodology pointer
  stub, methodology docs, pipeline commands, pipeline agents, skill
  templates, the `aide` MCP entry, the `aide-tree` launcher, and README —
  and never writes `.aide/config/brain.aide`, never writes the `.mcp.json`
  `brain` entry, never invokes `provisionBrain`, never creates the brain
  root directory, never asks for a brain path, and never accepts any
  brain-shaped flag (`--brain-path`, `--vault-path`, `--brain-root`, etc.)
  in its current shape. Brain wiring is fully delegated to
  `/aide:brain config` on the first `/aide` run. The post-install warning
  routes brain wiring to `/aide:brain config` (no `<BRAIN_PATH>`
  placeholder framing — there is no placeholder anymore). All tests for
  the retired flow are deleted; new tests assert the no-brain-surfaces
  contract end-to-end.
---

